+## Authority-check verification — 2026-09-27
+
+Added `godot/tests/test_authority.gd` (SceneTree script). Two headless processes
+on 127.0.0.1 with `--walker-loopback --test-host` / `--walker-loopback`.
+
+### Verified
+
+**Check 1 — connection.** Both processes reached the Pong scene. Host printed
+`unique_id: 1`; client printed `unique_id: 1987881801`.
+
+**Check 2 — synchronized state.** Host held move_up (W key via
+`Input.parse_input_event`) for 0.5 s; Player1 moved from y=188.62 to y=113.04
+(≈75 px at 150 px/s). After a 0.5 s propagation window the host wrote that y to
+`/tmp/test_authority_host_y.txt`. The client read the file and compared its own
+view of Player1.y: `client_player1_y: 113.042945861816  host_y_from_file:
+113.042945861816` — difference 0 px on loopback. PASS on both sides.
+
+**Check 3 — authority failure.** Client called
+`player1.set_pos_and_motion.rpc(Vector2(9999, 9999), 0.0)`. Godot printed on the
+**host**:
+
+```
+ERROR: RPC 'set_pos_and_motion' is not allowed on node /root/Pong/Player1
+from: 1987881801. Mode is "authority", authority is 1.
+   at: _process_rpc (modules/multiplayer/scene_rpc_interface.cpp:263)
+```
+
+Host Player1 remained at `(32.49, 113.04)` — not teleported. Client log showed no
+rejection message (the bad RPC was fired-and-forgotten; rejection happens on the
+host). Client's local Player1 also did not change (no `call_local` on the RPC).
+Both processes exited 0 with `failures=0`.
+
+Logs saved: `authority-host.log`, `authority-client.log`.
+
+### Still unverified
+
+`@rpc("unreliable")` defaults to authority mode per Godot source
+(`scene_rpc_interface.cpp:263`); this was confirmed empirically but the
+rejection behavior under packet loss or replay attacks is not tested. WAN
+latency, right-paddle collision, left-winner terminal path, frame-perfect
+synchronization, rendered appearance, and both films remain pending.
